# AI Route Planning & Optimization – Feature Rule

## Objective

Deliver a premium, interactive UI for AI-powered courier route planning and optimization, supporting both automated and manual workflows.  
**All UI must be accessible, responsive, and visually aligned with the Ashraf Courier Business Platform design system.**

---

## 1. Core Features

- **Interactive Map:**  
  - Display all delivery points (stops) on a Google Maps (or equivalent) map.
  - Each point must be clearly marked and accessible (keyboard, ARIA labels).
- **Route Visualization:**  
  - Draw the optimized route connecting all delivery points in order.
  - Show turn-by-turn directions in a sidebar or panel.
- **Estimated Delivery Times:**  
  - Display ETA for each stop, factoring in current traffic and stop order.
  - Show total route time and distance.
- **Traffic-Aware Routing:**  
  - Visually indicate traffic conditions on the route (e.g., color-coded segments).
  - Update ETAs and route if traffic data changes (mocked in UI phase).
- **Manual Route Adjustment:**  
  - Allow users to drag-and-drop stops to reorder deliveries.
  - Instantly update route, ETAs, and directions on adjustment.
  - Provide a “Re-optimize” button to let AI suggest the best route after manual changes.

---

## 2. UI/UX Requirements

- **Map Integration:**  
  - Use Google Maps JavaScript API (or mock for UI-only phase).
  - All map controls must be accessible and keyboard-navigable.
- **Directions Panel:**  
  - List each stop with address, ETA, and action buttons (e.g., “Mark as Delivered”).
  - Highlight the current/next stop.
- **Responsive Design:**  
  - Map and directions panel must adapt to mobile and desktop layouts.
- **Transitions & Animations:**  
  - Use premium, subtle transitions for map updates, panel slides, and drag-and-drop.
  - Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for accessibility.
- **Accessibility:**  
  - All interactive elements must have ARIA labels, keyboard support, and sufficient color contrast.
  - Test with screen readers and keyboard navigation.

---

## 3. Data & Logic

- **Mock Data:**  
  - Use static/mock data for delivery points, traffic, and ETAs in UI-only phase.
  - No backend/API integration at this stage.
- **State Management:**  
  - Use Zustand for client-side state if needed.
- **No Dead Code:**  
  - Remove all TODOs and commented-out code before submission.

---

## 4. Deliverables

- Fully functional, navigable UI for route planning and optimization.
- All features above implemented with mock/static data.
- README update with usage and testing instructions.

---

## 5. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a modern, accessible, and delightful route planning UI that sets the foundation for future AI and backend integration.